00:45:46.510 --> 00:45:48.879
The first Black American
to get elected to Congress.

00:45:48.879 --> 00:45:51.148
He was a Republican in 1870.

00:45:51.148 --> 00:45:52.282
You know, when the first

00:45:52.282 --> 00:45:53.550 align:start size:84% position:16%
Black American
Democrat was elected?

00:45:53.550 --> 00:45:55.219
60 years later.

00:45:55.219 --> 00:45:56.453
You know, Joseph Rainey

00:45:56.453 --> 00:45:57.988
wasn't the only black
Republican elected.

00:45:57.988 --> 00:46:00.090
A number of them were elected.

00:46:00.090 --> 00:46:02.826 align:start size:97% position:3%
So then we had a Presidential
race that was close.

00:46:02.826 --> 00:46:04.495 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so the Democrats
partnered with the Republicans

00:46:04.495 --> 00:46:07.898
and said, "You won, but
only on one condition.

00:46:07.898 --> 00:46:10.334
You removed the federal
troops from the South."

00:46:10.334 --> 00:46:11.902 align:start size:97% position:3%
And when they removed the
federal troops from the South,

00:46:11.902 --> 00:46:15.005
lo and behold, Democrats
then defeated Republicans.

00:46:15.005 --> 00:46:17.608
And what did they do when
they defeated Republicans?

00:46:17.608 --> 00:46:21.445
They changed the Election Law
and brought Jim Crow Laws in

00:46:21.445 --> 00:46:24.515
and picked people based
upon who can go there.

00:46:24.515 --> 00:46:29.019 align:start size:97% position:3%
Remember the Republican Party,
what it was founded upon.

00:46:29.019 --> 00:46:30.454
So when the Democrats,

00:46:30.454 --> 00:46:33.423 align:start size:97% position:3%
they removed five portraits
of Democrat speakers.

00:46:33.423 --> 00:46:34.858
Okay. You should.

00:46:34.858 --> 00:46:36.293 align:start size:84% position:16%
But every stature
they wanted to remove

00:46:36.293 --> 00:46:40.130 align:start size:84% position:16%
was of a Democrat sent
to us from a state

00:46:40.130 --> 00:46:42.766
that a Democrat majority
was in, that voted for it,

00:46:42.766 --> 00:46:44.368
that was accepted by a Congress,

00:46:44.368 --> 00:46:46.703 align:start size:84% position:16%
that was a majority
of Democrats.

00:46:46.703 --> 00:46:48.705 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, why do you
keep your name then?

00:46:48.705 --> 00:46:50.240
Change the name of the party.

00:46:50.240 --> 00:46:52.709
We don't have to change the
name of the Republican Party

00:46:52.709 --> 00:46:55.212
'cause we were founded on the
idea that we're all equal.

00:46:55.212 --> 00:46:58.816
We fought for the idea that
people were equal and fair.

00:46:58.816 --> 00:47:00.551 align:start size:84% position:16%
And at times I've
watched when you say,

00:47:00.551 --> 00:47:02.686
"How can you change?"

00:47:02.686 --> 00:47:04.188 align:start size:97% position:3%
They don't know the history.
- Yeah.

00:47:04.188 --> 00:47:06.156
- They don't know the story.

00:47:06.156 --> 00:47:07.624 align:start size:84% position:16%
And we need to
tell it more often.

00:47:07.624 --> 00:47:09.893 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So is that education
fundamentally?

00:47:09.893 --> 00:47:11.161 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean, is that
why we have to get

00:47:11.161 --> 00:47:12.663
the schools back more
than anything else,

00:47:12.663 --> 00:47:15.432
because people believe
now that 1619 project

00:47:15.432 --> 00:47:17.401
was, you know, the true
the story of America?

00:47:17.401 --> 00:47:18.936 align:start size:84% position:16%
- They tried to
recreate our history.

00:47:18.936 --> 00:47:22.105 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, the idea
that Columbus is bad,

00:47:23.473 --> 00:47:27.578
the idea that, you know,
you can't say Christmas,

00:47:28.745 --> 00:47:30.747
I mean mean our founders

00:47:31.915 --> 00:47:34.818 align:start size:88% position:13%
were some of the most
religious people, right.

00:47:34.818 --> 00:47:37.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
We believe in re
religious freedom though.

00:47:37.421 --> 00:47:39.423
I mean, the idea in our schools,

00:47:39.423 --> 00:47:42.025
what I'm most worried about is,

00:47:43.360 --> 00:47:46.763
nobody in the Taliban
or in the Chinese Army

00:47:46.763 --> 00:47:49.833 align:start size:97% position:3%
are worried about a pronoun.
(audience laughing)

00:47:49.833 --> 00:47:50.901
Nobody, okay.

00:47:52.069 --> 00:47:55.405
With all respect, they
just wanna fight to win.

00:47:55.405 --> 00:47:58.575 align:start size:97% position:3%
At the end of the day, we
may have the right pronouns,

00:47:58.575 --> 00:48:01.311 align:start size:84% position:16%
but if we lose the
war, we're out, right?

00:48:01.311 --> 00:48:02.980
And they only understand fear.

00:48:02.980 --> 00:48:05.682
But also, the idea
of our children.

00:48:05.682 --> 00:48:07.918 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm not worried about my kids
competing with your kids.

00:48:07.918 --> 00:48:12.122 align:start position:0%
I'm worried about our kids
competing with India and China.

00:48:12.122 --> 00:48:16.960 align:start position:0%
And the great equalizer in
America is the education system.

00:48:16.960 --> 00:48:19.029
And why it's the Democrats
who fight charter schools.

00:48:19.029 --> 00:48:21.365
And this is the other thing
that's so great about states.

00:48:21.365 --> 00:48:24.201
What Arizona has done,
what Florida has done

00:48:24.201 --> 00:48:27.404 align:start size:97% position:3%
that allows your tax dollars
to follow your students

00:48:27.404 --> 00:48:29.539
so they can go to
a better school.

00:48:29.539 --> 00:48:32.643 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's your choice, you
know. That's gonna change.

00:48:32.643 --> 00:48:35.078
And who does that help the most?

00:48:35.078 --> 00:48:37.314 align:start size:88% position:13%
Really those who are
lower income in America,

00:48:37.314 --> 00:48:40.951
and many times many more
minorities than others.

00:48:40.951 --> 00:48:42.486
I'll tell you, today
I was very excited.

00:48:42.486 --> 00:48:47.057
I had a school group that
was from my hometown here.

00:48:47.057 --> 00:48:49.293
And it's a charter school

00:48:49.293 --> 00:48:51.929
that was developed by this
one family, the Grimm's.

00:48:51.929 --> 00:48:54.631
Any of you ever eat
these baby carrots?

00:48:54.631 --> 00:48:55.799
Okay. They just sold.

00:48:55.799 --> 00:48:57.701 align:start size:88% position:13%
But there was two
families in my district

00:48:57.701 --> 00:49:00.437
that grew 80% of all the
carrots in the country.

00:49:00.437 --> 00:49:01.638
And you want a secret?

00:49:01.638 --> 00:49:02.506 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's no such thing
as a baby carrot.

00:49:02.506 --> 00:49:03.740
They're regular carrots.

00:49:03.740 --> 00:49:05.442
We chop 'em, charge you
more and you buy 'em.

00:49:05.442 --> 00:49:07.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
We love you for it, okay.
(audience laughing)

00:49:07.811 --> 00:49:10.347 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Goodnight, everybody.
(audience laughing)

00:49:10.347 --> 00:49:11.882 align:start size:84% position:16%
- But what they
were doing is that,

00:49:11.882 --> 00:49:13.550
they're a great
family, you know.

00:49:13.550 --> 00:49:15.118
These families that
owned businesses,

00:49:15.118 --> 00:49:16.887
and became a very big business,

00:49:16.887 --> 00:49:18.388
well, they would put
all this money away

00:49:18.388 --> 00:49:20.023
to give scholarships to
their employees' children

00:49:20.023 --> 00:49:21.458
to go to college and they found,

00:49:21.458 --> 00:49:22.726
well, you're not taking up.

00:49:22.726 --> 00:49:23.927
Well, they weren't
getting into college.

00:49:23.927 --> 00:49:25.963
They said, "Well, we
gotta go further down."

00:49:25.963 --> 00:49:27.464 align:start size:88% position:13%
Well, they found the
school district with it.

00:49:27.464 --> 00:49:30.067
So they were gonna pay to
put in a charter school.

00:49:30.067 --> 00:49:31.568
The school district fought 'em.

00:49:31.568 --> 00:49:33.236
But when they finally got
the charter school came in,

00:49:33.236 --> 00:49:38.241 align:start size:97% position:3%
and this is 90% will be
immigrants in this community.

00:49:38.976 --> 00:49:40.811
They wear uniforms,

00:49:40.811 --> 00:49:42.879
they take extra classes, right.

00:49:42.879 --> 00:49:44.414
And the thing I will tell you,

00:49:44.414 --> 00:49:45.849
in the first two years,

00:49:45.849 --> 00:49:47.351
this school scores are competing

00:49:47.351 --> 00:49:50.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the highest scores
of anywhere in the county.

00:49:50.587 --> 00:49:52.589
And we just had,
for the first time,

00:49:52.589 --> 00:49:53.991
the eighth graders been there,

00:49:53.991 --> 00:49:57.027 align:start position:0%
they just came and had a
picture with me in The Rotunda.

00:49:57.027 --> 00:49:59.529
And the excitement
on these kids' faces

00:49:59.529 --> 00:50:00.797
that one little girl stood up.

00:50:00.797 --> 00:50:02.632
You could tell that she
was the class President.

00:50:02.632 --> 00:50:04.167
She could ride up
on so and so on,

00:50:04.167 --> 00:50:05.802
I want a picture of you.

00:50:05.802 --> 00:50:08.772
And I'm thinking you're gonna
be Speaker one day, right.

00:50:08.772 --> 00:50:11.408 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, but how
proud an opportunity.

00:50:11.408 --> 00:50:13.043 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's the great
equalizer in America.

00:50:13.043 --> 00:50:14.678 align:start size:84% position:16%
We talk about
everybody being equal,

00:50:14.678 --> 00:50:17.180
but let's give 'em
an equal opportunity

00:50:17.180 --> 00:50:19.649
and let's not hold people back.

00:50:19.649 --> 00:50:20.951
- We got three minutes left

00:50:20.951 --> 00:50:22.819
and then you gotta
get back to work.

00:50:22.819 --> 00:50:25.522
So, I will ask you one
tough one at the end.

00:50:25.522 --> 00:50:29.259
You've talked a lot
about civility here.

00:50:29.259 --> 00:50:30.861 align:start size:84% position:16%
The audience obviously
knows my feelings

00:50:30.861 --> 00:50:34.698 align:start size:97% position:3%
about what's going on in
Florida and Governor DeSantis,

00:50:34.698 --> 00:50:35.966
Obviously, I supported Trump.

00:50:35.966 --> 00:50:39.236
Trump supported you
in the Speakership.

00:50:39.236 --> 00:50:43.173
This seems to be coming to
a head one way or another.

00:50:43.173 --> 00:50:45.909 align:start size:88% position:13%
I've been concerned
about the civility also

00:50:45.909 --> 00:50:48.945 align:start size:97% position:3%
because I don't wanna see
mutually assured destruction.

00:50:48.945 --> 00:50:50.514
If Trump ends up President

00:50:50.514 --> 00:50:52.182 align:start size:81% position:19%
and DeSantis stays
as my Governor,

00:50:52.182 --> 00:50:53.784
that'll be just fine with me.

00:50:53.784 --> 00:50:56.053
If DeSantis is President,
that'll be fine with me.

00:50:56.053 --> 00:50:57.587 align:start size:88% position:13%
But I don't want to
destroy the whole thing.

00:50:57.587 --> 00:51:00.290
And I sense we really
are in a dangerous spot

00:51:00.290 --> 00:51:02.192 align:start size:84% position:16%
where we have a
lot of the momentum

00:51:02.192 --> 00:51:03.727 align:start size:88% position:13%
that you've talked
about here and civility

00:51:03.727 --> 00:51:06.797
and the right ideas and
things of that nature.

00:51:06.797 --> 00:51:08.965 align:start size:84% position:16%
But it's like a
Tinder box in a way,

00:51:08.965 --> 00:51:11.001
maybe because of some
of the personalities.

00:51:11.001 --> 00:51:12.335
- I always think
we should do this.

00:51:12.335 --> 00:51:13.804
Whenever I sit down,

00:51:13.804 --> 00:51:16.106 align:start size:97% position:3%
like I was sitting down
with some members yesterday,

00:51:16.106 --> 00:51:17.441 align:start size:81% position:19%
we were talking
around each other.

00:51:17.441 --> 00:51:20.444
I said, "What do
we want to achieve?

00:51:21.511 --> 00:51:22.779 align:start size:88% position:13%
Okay, you take everybody
out of running.

00:51:22.779 --> 00:51:23.814
What do you want achieve?"

00:51:23.814 --> 00:51:26.016
You wanna stop the bad policies.

00:51:26.016 --> 00:51:29.319
So, you want somebody else
in the White House, right.

00:51:29.319 --> 00:51:30.654
So you gotta understand too,

00:51:30.654 --> 00:51:32.222
what's the debate
gonna be about?

00:51:32.222 --> 00:51:34.624 align:start size:84% position:16%
All the things
that Biden has done

00:51:34.624 --> 00:51:36.660
that somebody else
could do better.

00:51:36.660 --> 00:51:39.162
I think that resonates
more with the public.

00:51:39.162 --> 00:51:40.397
It gets more people to vote.

00:51:40.397 --> 00:51:43.033
It's about addition,
not subtraction, okay.

00:51:43.033 --> 00:51:45.102
And so it's tough when
you get in a competition.

00:51:45.102 --> 00:51:48.171
But members should really
see that whoever runs.

00:51:48.171 --> 00:51:49.706
And lots of times,

00:51:49.706 --> 00:51:51.575
whoever the front runner is
today is not the nominee.

00:51:51.575 --> 00:51:53.743
And whatever we think
the issue is today

00:51:53.743 --> 00:51:55.412 align:start size:81% position:19%
is probably not
gonna be the issue

00:51:55.412 --> 00:51:58.615
in another November from now.

00:51:58.615 --> 00:52:01.118 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I think the
Democratic policies

00:52:01.118 --> 00:52:03.487
will always be the issue, right.

00:52:03.487 --> 00:52:06.990
And I just don't
think the country

00:52:06.990 --> 00:52:09.493
wants another four
years of Joe Biden.

00:52:09.493 --> 00:52:11.795
I just don't believe
we can sustain that.

00:52:11.795 --> 00:52:14.131 align:start size:84% position:16%
And don't do damage
to one another

00:52:14.131 --> 00:52:15.365
that allows him to get in

00:52:15.365 --> 00:52:16.867
because they're gonna
give you a lot of bait.

00:52:16.867 --> 00:52:18.702
Don't take it.

00:52:18.702 --> 00:52:20.904 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Note, he did not
say Trump nor DeSantis

00:52:20.904 --> 00:52:22.139
in that entire thing.
(audience laughing)

00:52:22.139 --> 00:52:23.640
That was very slick.

00:52:23.640 --> 00:52:25.909
Guys, please make some noise
for the Speaker of the House,

00:52:25.909 --> 00:52:26.743
Kevin McCarthy.

00:52:26.743 --> 00:52:27.811
(audience applauding)

00:52:27.811 --> 00:52:29.212 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Thank you.
- Thank you, my friend.

